// Rule: [T1219][T1059.001][T1218.007] Dual RMM Abuse - MSP360 Powershell Msiexec
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1219, T1059.001, T1218.007
// Classification: Hunting query
// Status: Untested implementation sketch
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR / DeviceProcessEvents
// Required telemetry: DeviceProcessEvents
// Purpose: Hunts for MSP360 RMM Agent launching PowerShell and for PowerShell, with MSP360 as parent, launching an MSI from T emp.
// Logic: Evaluate DeviceProcessEvents for msp360 powershell msiexec using the existing source-derived conditions while preserving projected investigation context.
// A match proves: A result proves that the published query conditions matched in DeviceProcessEvents; it is an investigative event, not a malicious verdict.
// A match does not prove: phishing, malicious ScreenConnect use, or credential access.
// Expected false positives: authorized administration, approved software, testing, or benign artifact collisions.
// Coverage limits: local schema, field population, retention, collection scope, and attacker variation require validation.
// Evidence claims: C001, C002, C003
//
// Rule name: [T1219][T1059.001][T1218.007] MSP360 RMM Agent to PowerShell and MSIExec
// Hunting query - Untested implementation sketch
// Confidence: Medium
// Primary platform: Microsoft Defender XDR / DeviceProcessEvents
// Objective: identify the source-observed MSP360 RMM -> PowerShell -> MSI installation lineage.
// A match does not prove phishing, malicious ScreenConnect use, or credential access.
DeviceProcessEvents
| where
    (FileName =~ "powershell.exe"
        and InitiatingProcessFileName =~ "RMM.Agent.exe")
    or
    (FileName =~ "msiexec.exe"
        and InitiatingProcessFileName =~ "powershell.exe"
        and InitiatingProcessParentFileName =~ "RMM.Agent.exe"
        and ProcessCommandLine has "\\Temp\\"
        and ProcessCommandLine has ".msi")
| project Timestamp, DeviceId, DeviceName,
          FileName, FolderPath, ProcessCommandLine,
          ProcessId, ProcessUniqueId,
          AccountDomain, AccountName,
          InitiatingProcessFileName, InitiatingProcessFolderPath,
          InitiatingProcessCommandLine, InitiatingProcessId,
          InitiatingProcessUniqueId, InitiatingProcessParentFileName,
          ReportId
| order by Timestamp desc
